Twenty-five markets carried `verifiedAt: null` and were correctly excluded from
the service area, out of the API's service_area list, and reading "unconfirmed"
on their corridor pages while crews were working there. The owner confirmed
every one of them on 2026-09-10. Zero Ontario markets are unconfirmed. Zero are
corridor-target. The map is complete.

WHAT WAS NOT DONE, DELIBERATELY

No local content was invented. Not one housing note, not one signature project,
not one drive time or population figure. Twenty-seven of the forty-three still
have no CityContent and therefore still have no page, because worthiness.ts
requires real content independently of any confirmation and that gate did not
move. The fastest version of this change was twenty-five templated city pages
with the name swapped in; F-157 is this repository's own record of nearly
shipping exactly that, and it is the single most reliably punished pattern in
local search.

WHY THREE TIERS AND NOT ONE

Flattening forty-three markets into "core-active" would have thrown away the
most useful thing in the file. Twenty-eight are inside the daily-return radius.
Fifteen — the far Niagara belt, the 403/6 run to Kitchener, the north end of the
400, Kawartha Lakes — are a real drive, and their own sentence says so:
"scheduled as a trip, confirmed in advance, and priced with that in the written
quote." A customer in Port Colborne reading that is being told something true
that helps them decide. A customer in Port Colborne reading "routine daily
coverage" finds out it was not, on the morning nobody arrives.

verifiedBy

New field, on every confirmed record including the eighteen that came before.
`'owner'` means the owner of this business stated on that date what coverage of
that municipality means. It is NOT a record of documented completed work — that
is has_page, reported separately, and false for most confirmed markets. The API
publishes a confirmation_basis paragraph saying so in the payload, because
conflating the two is how a coverage list quietly becomes a portfolio it has
not earned.

THE GUARD, WHICH WENT BLIND AND WAS FIXED PROPERLY

verify-geo named ACTIVE, TORONTO_TRUTH and UNVERIFIED literally. Adding
COVERED() and BY_TRIP() blinded it instantly — twenty-five records it could not
classify. Had its fallback been "assume confirmed" rather than "report
unreadable", it would have passed while asserting coverage nobody had made. It
now derives the confirming constructors from the file: any helper whose body
sets verifiedAt to anything but null confirms. A new constructor is classified
by what it does, the day it is written.

Three new checks, four regressions, all fired:
  · an operational status with no dated confirmation — a coverage claim with
    nobody behind it
  · a confirmed market still labelled corridor-target — coverage the business
    has and is not claiming
  · a confirmation with no attribution
  · the reader going blind again

63 guards green, 296 tests, tsc at its 115-error baseline with nothing new.

